{"id":"word:hebrew:H5922","type":"word","title":"עַל","subtitle":"H5922 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"about, against, concerning, for, (there-) fore, from, in, × more, of, (there-, up-) on, (in-) to, why with.","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עַל (H5922) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: prep.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 111 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עַל (ʻal) means about, against, concerning, for, (there-) fore, from, in, × more, of, (there-, up-) on, (in-) to, why with. First listed occurrence: Dan 2 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עַל","transliteration":"ʻal","pronunciation":"al","strong":"H5922","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5922","partOfSpeech":"prep","forms":["עַל","עַֽל","עלי/ך","וְ/עַל","עֲלֽוֹ/הִי"],"morphs":[["AR",64],["AR/Sp2ms",13],["AR/Sp3ms",13],["AC/R",7],["AR/Sp1cs",4],["AR/Sp1cp",3],["AR/Sp3mp",3],["AR/Sp3fs",2],["AR/Sp3cs",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"about, against, concerning, for, (there-) fore, from, in, × more, of, (there-, up-) on, (in-) to, why with.","usage":"about, against, concerning, for, (there-) fore, from, in, × more, of, (there-, up-) on, (in-) to, why with.","full":"H5922. al עַל preposition upon, over, on account of, above, to, against (Biblical Hebrew and General Aramaic id. ); — suffix 1 singular עֲלַי ; 2 masculine singular עליך Kt (so Egyptian Aramaic, Cooke No. 77, A 5, 6, B 8 , S-C Pap. A 3, B 5 +), עֲלָךְ , Qr ( עֲלַךְ ᵑ7 , Dalm § 47, 2 ) Dan 3:12 6 t. Daniel; Ezra 7:18 ; 3 masculine singular עֲלוֺהִי (so Nabataean, Palmyrene; Egyptian Aramaic עלוי S-C A 6 +) Dan 3:28 +, עֲלֹהִי Ezra 6:11 ; 3 feminine singular עליה Kt (so Egyptian Aramaic, S-C D 24 ), עֲלַהּ Qr (so ᵑ7 ) Dan 4:14 ; 5:21 ; 1 plural עֲלֵינָא Ezra 4:12 , עֲלֵ֑ינָא 4:18 ; 5:17 Baer (Gi עֲלֶ֑ינָא ); 3 masculine plural עֲלֵיהֹם (so Nabataean, CIS ii. 226 ; Egyptian Aramaic, S-C Pap. F 5, 8 +) 7:24 , עֲלֵיהוֺן 5:1 , 3 ; &#8212; 1. a. upon , Dan 2:10 , 28 , 46 ; 5:5 , 7 ; 6:11 + often, 4:26 מַלְכוּתָא עַלהֵֿיכַל ( 2Sam 11:2 ); to be established מַלְכוּתִי עַל 2 Samuel 4:33 (compare 2Chr 1:1 ; Biblical Hebrew II. 1) to lay an impost upon , Ezra 7:24 ; to trust on , Dan 3:28 ; after a verb of motion, עַל מְטָא to come upon , 4:21 ; 4:25 ; of times, to pass over , 4:13 ; 4:20 ; 4:22 ; 4:29 ; Ezra 5:1 עֲלֵיהוֺן יִשְׂרָאֵל אֱלָהּ בְּשֻׁם i.e. (named) over them. b. idiomatic (as in Biblical Hebrew; see II. 1 d ) of the person who is the subject of an emotion or experience, Dan 5:9 עֲלוֺהִי שָׁנַיִן וְזִיוֺתִי were changed upon him, 7:28 ; 6:19 עֲלוֺהִי נַדַּת וְשִׁנְּתֵהּ (compare 2:1 ). c. on accusative of (Biblical Hebrew 1f b), Dan 3:16 עַלדְּֿנָה מִּתְגָּם . So in עַלדְּֿנָה on this accusative Ezra 4:15 , 22 ; 5:17 , עַלמָֿה wherefore ? Dan 2:15 ; and דִּי דִּבְרַת עַל (see ׳דְּ ). d. on behalf of ( ib. 1f c ), Ezra 6:17 . e. regarding, concerning ( ib. 1f g ), Dan 2:18 ; 5:14 , 29 ; 6:6 ; 6:13 ; Ezra 7:14 +? 2 over , with verbs of ruling, appointing, etc., Dan 2:48-49 , 3:12 ; 4:14 +, Ezra 4:20 ; 6:18 . 3 in a comparative sense, above, beyond , Dan 3:19 ; 6:4 . 4 expressing direction: a. to , of a person, after a verb of motion (compare Biblical Hebrew 7c a a), Dan 2:24 ; 4:31 ; 4:33 ; 6:7 ; 6:16 ; Ezra 4:12 , 23 + often; after to send (a letter, etc.) 4:11 , 17 , 18 ; 5:6 +, write 4:7 , prophesy 5:1 ; of the direction of the mind ( ib. 7c c ), Dan 3:12 ; 6:14 (twice in verse); 6:15 ; compare Ezra 5:5 אֱל ׳וְעֵין עַל הֲוַת (compare Jer 40:4 and אֶל Psa 34:16 ). b. against , Dan 3:19 , 29 ; 5:23 ; 6:5 ; 6:6 +; Ezra 4:8 ; 7:23 . 5 in such phrases as טְאֵב עַל, שְׁפַר (to be) good or acceptable to (as in Syriac and late Hebrew: see Biblical Hebrew 8 ), Ezra 5:17 טָב מַלְכָּא עַל אִם , 7:18 (twice in verse); Dan 4:24 ( יִשְׁמַּר ), 6:15 ( בְּאֵשׁ ), 6:24 ( טְאֵב ). — compare the synopsis of meanings in Lzb 340 .","rootNote":"(Aramaic) corresponding to 5921","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Dan 2 10","keyReferences":["Dan 2 10","Dan 2 15","Dan 2 18","Dan 2 24","Dan 2 28","Dan 2 29","Dan 2 30","Dan 2 34"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":111,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Dan 2 10","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 15","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 18","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 24","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 28","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַֽל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 29","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 30","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 34","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 46","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":46,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 48","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":48,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 48","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":48,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 2 49","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַ֤ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 3 12","book":"Dan","chapter":3,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עַל","source":"hebrew","morph":"AR"},{"reference":"Dan 3 12","book":"Dan","chapter":3,"verse":12,"en